      "hints": [
        "General term in $\\left(2x + \\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^6$ is $\\binom{6}{r}(2x)^{6-r}\\left(\\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}4^{-r} x^{6-3r}$.",
        "Set $6 - 3r = 0 \\implies r = 2$ to find the constant term."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write down the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x + \\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^6$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{6}{r}(2x)^{6-r}\\left(\\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^r = \\binom{6}{r}2^{6-r}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^r x^{6-3r}$$",
        "Set the power of $x$ equal to zero ($6 - 3r = 0 \\implies 3r = 6 \\implies r = 2$) to isolate the constant term:\n$$T_3 = \\binom{6}{2}(2x)^4\\left(\\frac{1}{4x^2}\\right)^2 = 15(16x^4)\\left(\\frac{1}{16x^4}\\right) = 15$$",
        "State the term independent of $x$:\n$$\\text{Term independent of } x = 15$$"
      ],
